IMPORT prelude

-- Medical and Elderly Care Endowment Schemes Act 2000 (Singapore) -- who may apply to Medifund and on whose behalf (ss 15, 16,
-- 17), what happens to a Medifund Account when a committee is dissolved or a hospital is wound up (s 12), the Medifund Account
-- accounting calendar (s 13), what "step-down care" is (s 2), when an ElderCare subvention may be paid to a provider (ss 22, 24,
-- 25(6)), revocation and suspension of a provider's approval and the sanction procedure (ss 25, 29), providers' record-keeping
-- duties (s 31), disclosure of medical information by authorised officers (s 43(2)), and the offences (ss 31, 38, 40, 41, 45).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 5/12/2025), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/MECESA2000.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December
-- 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the body is Act 19 of 2025 (deleting s 25(1)(c), wef 05/12/2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0074: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life relevance. The requirement
-- asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED to what a
-- patient (Medifund) and a step-down care provider (ElderCare Fund) meet. Not encoded: the constitution and investment of the two
-- Funds (ss 3, 4, 18-20), the uses of income (ss 5, 21) beyond their effect on subventions, the Advisory Council and the
-- Schedule, approval of institutions (s 8), grant conditions to committees (ss 9-11), the amount and conditions of subventions
-- (ss 26-28, which are left entirely to the Minister), monitoring powers (s 32) beyond the s 40(2) offence, the general financial
-- provisions (ss 33-39) beyond the s 38 offence, service (s 44), regulations (s 46) and transitional provisions (s 47). Any
-- "prescribed" requirement (s 15(1)(d), the means test) is taken as a single yes/no fact: no regulations were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Medical and Elderly Care Endowment Schemes Act 2000`

§§ `15 -- who may apply to Medifund`

-- s 15(1): "Every person who -- (a) is a citizen of Singapore; (b) has received treatment or requires treatment from any approved
-- institution; (c) is unable to pay the hospital charges, fees or other expenses incurred by the person; and (d) satisfies such
-- other requirements as may be prescribed, may apply to the Medifund committee designated ..."
DECLARE Patient HAS
    `is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has received or requires treatment from an approved institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is unable to pay the charges` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfies the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is incapacitated from applying` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the patient` IS A Patient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an eligible patient` IF
        `the patient`'s `is a citizen of Singapore`
    AND `the patient`'s `has received or requires treatment from an approved institution`
    AND `the patient`'s `is unable to pay the charges`
    AND `the patient`'s `satisfies the prescribed requirements`

§§ `16 -- applying on the patient's behalf`

-- s 16: "If an eligible patient, by reason of incapacity by physical or mental illness or any other cause, is unable to make an
-- application under section 15, any member of the patient's immediate family or the medical social worker in charge of the
-- patient's case may submit the application on the patient's behalf."
-- The Act names no one else (a friend, a hospital doctor) and does not say who may apply for a patient who is NOT incapacitated.
DECLARE Applicant IS ONE OF
    `the patient personally`
    `a member of the immediate family`
    `the medical social worker in charge of the case`
    `a friend of the patient`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant, `the patient` IS A Patient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may submit the application` IF
        `is an eligible patient` `the patient`
    AND CONSIDER `the applicant`
        WHEN `the patient personally` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a member of the immediate family` THEN `the patient`'s `is incapacitated from applying`
        WHEN `the medical social worker in charge of the case` THEN `the patient`'s `is incapacitated from applying`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `17 -- payment is discretionary`

-- s 17(1): the committee "may, if it thinks fit and subject to the availability of moneys in the Medifund Account -- (a) approve
-- the application ... and (b) authorise in writing payments of such amount as it thinks fit ... to the approved institution".
-- s 17(5): "Nothing in this Act is to be construed to require a Medifund committee ... to approve the application of every patient
-- who satisfies the requirements under section 15."
-- So payment goes to the INSTITUTION, not the patient, and eligibility is never sufficient.
GIVEN `the patient` IS A Patient, `moneys are available in the Medifund Account` IS A BOOLEAN, `the committee thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee may authorise a payment` IF
        `is an eligible patient` `the patient`
    AND `moneys are available in the Medifund Account`
    AND `the committee thinks fit`

GIVEN `the patient` IS A Patient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee is bound to approve` IF FALSE

§§ `12 -- Medifund Account moneys on dissolution or liquidation`

-- s 12(1): moneys in a Medifund Account "(a) are deemed not to form part of the property of the Medifund committee or approved
-- institution if the committee is dissolved or the institution goes into voluntary or compulsory liquidation; and (b) are not
-- available for payment of the debts of the Medifund committee or approved institution or liable to be paid or taken under or
-- pursuant to an enforcement order or process of any court."
-- s 12(2): on dissolution of the committee, the moneys, "after deduction of any payment to the approved institution which has been
-- authorised under section 17", are vested in and paid into the Medifund.
GIVEN `the money is in a Medifund Account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the money is available to the institution's creditors` IF
    NOT `the money is in a Medifund Account`

GIVEN `balance` IS A NUMBER, `authorised payments` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount returned to the Medifund on dissolution` MEANS
    IF `authorised payments` AT LEAST `balance` THEN 0
    ELSE `balance` MINUS `authorised payments`

§§ `13 -- the Medifund Account accounting calendar`

-- s 13(3): "The accounting period of a Medifund Account begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
-- s 13(2): financial statements are to be submitted to the auditor "as soon as practicable after the close of the accounting
-- period ... but not later than 30 June of each year".
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year its accounting period began` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `year` ELSE `year` MINUS 1

-- The year (on 30 June) by which the statements covering a transaction must reach the auditor. Inference: the "30 June of each
-- year" deadline is read as 30 June following the 31 March close.
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 30 June deadline year` MEANS
    `the year its accounting period began` `year` `month` PLUS 1

§§ `2 -- step-down care`

-- s 2(1): "step-down care" means "(a) accommodation, personal care and health care for any person suffering or recovering from any
-- sickness, disability or injury; (b) personal care and health care during the day for any such person; or (c) such other forms of
-- health care or care arrangements as the Minister may prescribe".
-- s 2(2): step-down care "is not taken to include any medical or health care provided in any maternity home or premises used or
-- intended to be used for the accommodation of pregnant women or of women immediately after childbirth".
DECLARE Care IS ONE OF
    `residential nursing care for a person recovering from a stroke`
    `day rehabilitation for a person with a disability`
    `a prescribed care arrangement`
    `care in a maternity home`
    `housing for a healthy retiree`

GIVEN `the care` IS A Care
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is step-down care` IF
    CONSIDER `the care`
    WHEN `residential nursing care for a person recovering from a stroke` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `day rehabilitation for a person with a disability` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a prescribed care arrangement` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `22, 24, 25(6) -- when a subvention may be paid`

-- s 22: subvention "cannot be made ... to any person providing step-down care unless the person is an approved provider" in
-- respect of the care (all types, specific types, at specific premises, or specific types at specific premises).
-- s 24: approval ceases if revoked or if "the period (if any) to which the approval is limited under section 23(6) expires".
-- s 25(6): while a suspension is in force the organisation "is not ... regarded as an approved provider, but on expiry of the
-- suspension, the organisation immediately reverts to being an approved provider".
DECLARE Provider HAS
    `is approved for this care at these premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approval revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approval period expired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `suspension in force` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the provider` IS A Provider
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is regarded as an approved provider` IF
        `the provider`'s `is approved for this care at these premises`
    AND (NOT `the provider`'s `approval revoked`)
    AND (NOT `the provider`'s `approval period expired`)
    AND (NOT `the provider`'s `suspension in force`)

GIVEN `the provider` IS A Provider, `the care` IS A Care
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a subvention may be paid` IF
        `is step-down care` `the care`
    AND `is regarded as an approved provider` `the provider`

§§ `25 -- revocation and suspension of approval`

-- s 25(1): the Minister may revoke, "or suspend for a period not exceeding 6 months", an approval if (a) the organisation has
-- ceased to be suitable; (b) the application contained false or misleading information in a material particular; (c) [Deleted by
-- Act 19 of 2025]; (ca) its Healthcare Services Act 2020 licence is revoked or suspended or ceases; (cb) its HCSA approval for the
-- premises, conveyance or service delivery mode is cancelled or suspended or ceases; (d) it is convicted of an offence under
-- s 31(3) or (5); (e) it fails to comply with the terms or conditions of the approval; or (f) it fails to comply with conditions of
-- a subvention "and the Minister is of the opinion that the organisation is again likely to so fail to comply".
-- A conviction under s 41 (false information) is not itself a listed ground; the encoding treats it as none, though the Minister
-- might reach the same result through (a) "ceased to be suitable" or, for the application itself, (b).
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `ceased to be suitable`
    `false or misleading application`
    `HCSA licence revoked or suspended`
    `HCSA approval for the premises cancelled`
    `convicted under section 31(3) or (5)`
    `convicted under section 41`
    `breach of approval conditions`
    `breach of subvention conditions`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `likely to fail again` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a ground to revoke or suspend` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `convicted under section 41` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `breach of subvention conditions` THEN `likely to fail again`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension length is within the power` IF
    `months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `months` AT MOST 6

-- s 25(2)(b): written submissions "within 7 days after receiving the notice, or any further period that the Minister may allow".
-- s 25(3): the Minister notifies the decision "within 7 days after the end of the period allowed ... for making submissions".
-- s 25(4): the revocation or suspension takes effect "(a) if no submission was made ... on the day after the last day for making
-- submissions; or (b) if such submission was made -- 7 days after the day on which the notice under subsection (3) was given".
-- s 29(2)-(4) lays down the same timetable for sanctions on a non-compliant provider, so the same functions serve both.
-- Days are counted as day numbers; "within 7 days after" day D is read as ending on day D + 7 (an inference: the Act has no
-- computation-of-time rule of its own, and the Interpretation Act was not consulted).
GIVEN `notice received` IS A NUMBER, `extension days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day for submissions` MEANS
    `notice received` PLUS 7 PLUS `extension days`

GIVEN `notice received` IS A NUMBER, `extension days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day for the decision notice` MEANS
    `the last day for submissions` `notice received` `extension days` PLUS 7

GIVEN `notice received` IS A NUMBER, `extension days` IS A NUMBER, `submission made` IS A BOOLEAN, `decision notice given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day the revocation or sanction takes effect` MEANS
    IF `submission made`
    THEN `decision notice given` PLUS 7
    ELSE `the last day for submissions` `notice received` `extension days` PLUS 1

§§ `29 -- sanctions for non-compliance`

-- s 29(1): for non-compliance "with section 31(1) or with any condition of any subvention", the Minister may "(a) revoke or suspend
-- the approval ...; (b) restrict the approval ...; (c) reduce the total amount of subvention payable ... in any subsequent payment
-- period; (d) require repayment of part or all of the subvention paid".
-- s 31(2) (audited annual statements) is NOT among the s 29 triggers, although failing it is an offence under s 31(3).
DECLARE Breach IS ONE OF
    `records not kept or retained under section 31(1)`
    `subvention condition breached`
    `audited statements not submitted under section 31(2)`

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 29 sanction is available` IF
    CONSIDER `the breach`
    WHEN `audited statements not submitted under section 31(2)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `31 -- providers' records`

-- s 31(1)(b): each record is retained "for a period ending 3 years (or such other period as an authorised officer may allow) after
-- the close of the financial year in which the record was made". The Act does not define a provider's financial year (s 34 sets
-- only the Funds' years), so the close is taken as a given.
GIVEN `years since the close of the financial year` IS A NUMBER, `officer allowed a shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the record may be discarded` IF
    `officer allowed a shorter period` OR `years since the close of the financial year` AT LEAST 3

§§ `43(2) -- disclosure of medical information`

-- s 43(2): an authorised officer "must not disclose any information which is contained in the medical records, or which relates to
-- the condition, treatment or diagnosis, of any person" unless "(a) under or for the purpose of administering and enforcing this
-- Act or the Infectious Diseases Act 1976; (b) for the purpose of any disciplinary proceedings under the Medical Registration Act
-- 1997; or (c) for any other purpose with the consent of the person to whom the information relates or the representative".
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `enforcing this Act`
    `enforcing the Infectious Diseases Act 1976`
    `Medical Registration Act disciplinary proceedings`
    `a newspaper story`
    `an insurer's claim review`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `the person consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may disclose medical information` IF
        `the person consented`
    OR  CONSIDER `the purpose`
        WHEN `enforcing this Act` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `enforcing the Infectious Diseases Act 1976` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Medical Registration Act disciplinary proceedings` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `31(3), (5), 38, 40, 41 -- offences and penalties`

-- s 31(3): failing s 31(1) or (2) -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000". s 31(5): a false or misleading record -- "$3,000".
-- s 38(2): failing an auditor's requirement, without reasonable excuse -- "$1,000".
-- s 40(1): obstructing an authorised officer -- "$5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both".
-- s 40(2): failing, without reasonable excuse, to answer or produce under s 32(1) -- "$2,000".
-- s 41: knowingly or recklessly giving false or misleading information -- "$5,000 or ... 12 months or ... both".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `provider failing to keep records or submit audited statements`
    `provider making a false record`
    `failing an auditor's requirement`
    `obstructing an authorised officer`
    `failing to answer an authorised officer`
    `knowingly giving false information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `provider failing to keep records or submit audited statements` THEN 2000
    WHEN `provider making a false record` THEN 3000
    WHEN `failing an auditor's requirement` THEN 1000
    WHEN `obstructing an authorised officer` THEN 5000
    WHEN `failing to answer an authorised officer` THEN 2000
    WHEN `knowingly giving false information` THEN 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing an authorised officer` THEN 12
    WHEN `knowingly giving false information` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 41 requires that the person acted "knowingly or recklessly"; an innocent error is not the offence.
GIVEN `information was false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN, `recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a section 41 offence` IF
    `information was false in a material particular` AND (`knowingly` OR `recklessly`)

§§ `45 -- officers of a body that offends`

-- s 45(1): a director, manager, partner, secretary or similar officer "shall also be guilty of that offence ... unless the person
-- proves that -- (a) the offence was committed without his or her consent or connivance; and (b) the person had exercised all such
-- diligence to prevent the commission of the offence as he or she ought to have exercised". Both limbs are needed.
GIVEN `the body committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `was an officer at the time` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
        `the body committed an offence`
    AND `was an officer at the time`
    AND (NOT (`proved no consent or connivance` AND `proved due diligence`))
